            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0730" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-04T13:00:00+08:00">June 4, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 4—2:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. A representative of Greater Shanghai and the Shanghai Municipal Council
                    initialed a <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> this morning covering
                    extra-Settlement roads and other questions. The agreement will not be published
                    until it has been offered to Municipal Council and the Chinese Government for
                    approval. I shall comment on the agreement in the next few days.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
